{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LcMCRUzpmjK2MgMZFRJnyj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: \"25%稀疏度放大SFT gap至显著水平，GRPO collapse在两个模型上均加速，三条claim完整成立。RASP既是SFT最优方法又是RLVR collapse诊断工具，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff跨模型跨稀疏度一致。投EMNLP Main无需降档。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K eval baseline + pruned models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"N=1319 full eval for unpruned baseline, RASP_20 post-prune, Standard_20 post-prune\"\n    expected_results:\n      unpruned_baseline_accuracy: 0.8127\n      rasp_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.29\n      standard_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.27\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 2.0\n      n_total: 1319\n    result_rationale: \"已有N=100数据确认RASP 31% vs Standard 27%。N=1319仅收窄CI（±2.4pp），点估计不变。Post-prune gap ~2pp不显著，因为pruning damage尚未通过SFT recovery放大差异。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Post-Prune Accuracy (20% structured, N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Model, Accuracy, 95% CI]\n        rows:\n          - [Unpruned, \"81.27%\", \"±2.1pp\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"29.0%\", \"±2.4pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"±2.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing massive accuracy drop from pruning (81→29/27%) with overlapping CIs between RASP and Standard\"\n    analysis: \"Post-prune差异不显著证实pruning damage本身不区分方法，真正差异在recovery阶段才显现。\"\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K eval all recovered models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"N=1319 eval for RASP_20 SFT, Standard_20 SFT, RASP_20 GRPO, Standard_20 GRPO, unpruned GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n      standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n      rasp_20_grpo_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n      standard_20_grpo_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n      unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n      sft_gap_rasp_vs_standard_pp: 2.2\n      grpo_delta_rasp_pp: -0.84\n      grpo_delta_standard_pp: -0.38\n      grpo_delta_unpruned_pp: 0.0\n    result_rationale: \"已有完整数据。GRPO对所有模型accuracy无正增益（unpruned完全相同1072/1319），pruned模型略降。paper Table 1核心数据已齐全。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Recovery Accuracy (GSM8K, N=1319, greedy)\"\n        columns: [Config, SFT, GRPO, \"Δ(GRPO-SFT)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Unpruned, \"81.27%\", \"81.27%\", \"+0.00pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"59.29%\", \"58.91%\", \"-0.38pp\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"61.49%\", \"60.65%\", \"-0.84pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for 3 configs, showing GRPO never improves accuracy\"\n    analysis: \"GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling是universal的；pruning-specific failure是training collapse而非accuracy degradation。\"\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune baseline 20% full pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO. ACL 2026 SOTA external baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      postprune_accuracy: 0.07\n      postprune_eos_rate: 0.02\n      post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n      post_sft_stderr: 0.027\n      post_sft_n1319_accuracy: 0.40\n      grpo_collapse_step: 3\n      grpo_peak_reward: 0.012\n      grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n    result_rationale: \"GRASP post-prune仅7%（已验证），SFT恢复至41%（已验证，p=0.001 vs Standard 64%）。GRASP激进剪枝破坏更多结构冗余，GRPO应在≤5步collapse——比RASP更快。GRASP removes high-gradient structures regardless of functional redundancy，resulting in maximal RLVR instability。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse Step]\n        rows:\n          - [GRASPrune, \"7%\", \"41%\", \"~3\"]\n          - [RASP, \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"~10\"]\n          - [Standard, \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"~60\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Collapse dynamics 4-line plot: GRASPrune(step3) < RASP(step10) < Standard(step60) < Unpruned(never). 严重度梯度完整。\"\n    analysis: \"GRASPrune的gradient-based选择策略去除了最多functional redundancy，验证了collapse速度∝redundancy removal程度。四点梯度使诊断工具framing更convincing。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune evaluation with 5 seeds for robust variance estimation\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.295\n      rasp_20_std: 0.012\n      standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.270\n      standard_20_std: 0.015\n      rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.03\n      seeds: [42, 123, 456, 789, 1024]\n      n_per_seed: 1319\n    result_rationale: \"Post-prune eval是deterministic（greedy decoding），seed影响仅来自calibration data sampling。RASP的CKA scoring对calibration data更稳定（因为CKA captures structural而非instance-level信号），故std略低。5-seed下2.5pp gap可达p<0.05。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Accuracy\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Mean±Std\", \"95% CI\", Seeds]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, \"29.5±1.2%\", \"[27.1, 31.9]\", 5]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0±1.5%\", \"[24.0, 30.0]\", 5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot with 5 seeds per method, showing RASP略高且方差更小\"\n    analysis: \"Post-prune gap达到marginal significance (p=0.03)，但核心论点不依赖此——真正差异在recovery和collapse dynamics。Multi-seed确认pruning本身reproducible。\"\n\n  - name: \"Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Ablation pruning at 20%: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random. Isolate CKA contribution\"\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_postprune: 0.25\n      gradient_only_postprune: 0.28\n      random_postprune: 0.15\n      magnitude_sft_recovery: 0.56\n      gradient_sft_recovery: 0.58\n      random_sft_recovery: 0.42\n      magnitude_grpo_collapse_step: 40\n      gradient_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n      random_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n    result_rationale: \"Magnitude-only保留大权重但忽略功能冗余，post-prune与Standard(importance-based)接近。Gradient-only与GRASPrune逻辑相似但无budget约束，略好于magnitude。Random是lower bound。CKA的贡献在于：RASP(31%)>gradient(28%)>magnitude(25%)>random(15%)。GRPO collapse速度中，random最快（随机破坏冗余路径），magnitude/gradient因保留high-importance units而较慢，但仍比Standard快（Standard的importance metric隐式保留了部分冗余）。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Scoring Ablation Results\"\n        columns: [Scoring, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP (I×(1-F)^α), \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"step ~10\"]\n          - [Standard (importance), \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"step ~60\"]\n          - [Gradient-only, \"28%\", \"58%\", \"step ~45\"]\n          - [Magnitude-only, \"25%\", \"56%\", \"step ~40\"]\n          - [Random, \"15%\", \"42%\", \"step ~8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: post-prune accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all methods, showing RASP is Pareto-dominated point — high SFT but fast collapse\"\n    analysis: \"CKA贡献体现在SFT recovery（+5pp over magnitude），但对GRPO有害（collapse比magnitude/gradient快4-6×）。验证redundancy removal与collapse速度的因果关系。\"\n\n  - name: \"Per-structure CKA-recoverability correlation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"Per-head F(h) correlated with activation change post-recovery. Mixed-effects regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      fh_recovery_correlation_sft: -0.42\n      fh_recovery_correlation_sft_p: 0.001\n      fh_collapse_speed_correlation: 0.55\n      fh_collapse_speed_p: 0.0003\n      mixed_effects_r2: 0.38\n      layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n      controlling_for_weight_norm: true\n      controlling_for_gradient_importance: true\n      n_structures: 784\n    result_rationale: \"F(h)（CKA功能冗余度）高的结构在SFT后activation变化小（r=-0.42）——因为它们的功能已由其他结构承接，不需要恢复。但高F(h)结构的移除与GRPO collapse速度正相关（r=0.55）——因为它们提供的backup paths是RL exploration的安全网。Mixed-effects R²=0.38说明F(h)解释了显著但非全部方差（其他因素如layer position也重要）。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CKA-Recoverability Regression\"\n        columns: [Predictor, β, SE, p-value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\", -0.42, 0.08, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"Weight norm\", 0.12, 0.05, 0.02]\n          - [\"Gradient importance\", 0.08, 0.06, 0.18]\n          - [\"Layer (random)\", \"σ²=0.15\", \"-\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter with regression line: F(h) vs activation change magnitude (left panel, SFT context), F(h) vs time-to-collapse contribution (right panel, GRPO context)\"\n    analysis: \"机制验证：高冗余结构SFT可安全移除（功能可redistribution），但GRPO需要它们作为exploration buffer。这是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的结构层面证据。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT-only recovery comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Same pruned models, SFT only (no GRPO stage). Tests whether pruning strategy优劣在SFT-only pipeline中成立\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.6149\n      standard_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5929\n      gap_pp: 2.2\n      p_value: 0.25\n      rasp_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.57\n      standard_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5125\n      gap_25_pp: 5.75\n      p_25_value: 0.008\n    result_rationale: \"20%稀疏度下SFT gap仅2.2pp（已有数据，p=0.25不显著）。25%稀疏度放大效应：Standard在更高稀疏度下丢失更多关键结构，SFT难以完全恢复；RASP的CKA-aware选择在25%时保留了更关键的functional units，使recovery gap扩大至5.75pp（p=0.008）。这验证了'SFT下RASP优越性随稀疏度单调递增'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SFT-Only Recovery by Sparsity\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, RASP SFT, Standard SFT, Gap, p-value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", \"61.49%\", \"59.29%\", \"+2.2pp\", 0.25]\n          - [\"25%\", \"57.0%\", \"51.25%\", \"+5.75pp\", 0.008]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: accuracy vs sparsity for RASP and Standard, diverging as sparsity increases. Error bars show CI narrowing at N=1319.\"\n    analysis: \"SFT gap在25%处achieve significance。Claim 3直接支持：SFT-only pipeline下RASP显著优于Standard，但GRPO pipeline下RASP有害——pruning策略的最优性conditioned on recovery method。\"\n\n  - name: \"25% sparsity full pipeline (RASP + Standard)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25% structured pruning: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both methods. Core scope expansion.\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_postprune: 0.21\n      standard_25_postprune: 0.16\n      rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.57\n      standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n      sft_gap_pp: 5.75\n      sft_gap_p_value: 0.008\n      grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n      grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.025\n      grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.97\n      grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 20\n      grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.055\n      grpo_standard_25_step60_frac_zero_std: 0.85\n      collapse_ratio_standard_vs_rasp: 5.0\n    result_rationale: \"25%稀疏度下两个关键放大效应：(1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大至5.75pp，因为Standard在更高稀疏度下不得不移除更多functionally important structures（importance ranking的long tail quality下降），而RASP的CKA-aware selection依然能识别truly redundant structures。(2) GRPO collapse加速：RASP从step10→step4（冗余路径更少，RL exploration更快失去safety net），Standard从step60→step20（相同逻辑但程度较轻）。Collapse ratio从6x(20%)收缩至5x(25%)因为Standard也开始受损严重。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 25% Sparsity Pipeline Results\"\n        columns: [Method, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse, GRPO Δ vs SFT]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_25, \"21%\", \"57.0%\", \"step 4\", \"-1.5pp\"]\n          - [Standard_25, \"16%\", \"51.25%\", \"step 20\", \"-2.0pp\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Collapse Dynamics Comparison (20% vs 25%)\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Collapse@20%\", \"Collapse@25%\", Acceleration]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, \"step 10\", \"step 4\", \"2.5×\"]\n          - [Standard, \"step 60\", \"step 20\", \"3×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel: (Left) SFT accuracy vs sparsity showing divergence at 25%. (Right) frac_zero_std curves at 25% showing RASP collapse at step 4 vs Standard at step 20.\"\n    analysis: \"25%是paper的sweet spot：SFT gap达到显著，GRPO collapse更极端，所有效应放大。这使三条claim全部有strong statistical backing。\"\n\n  - name: \"30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30% prune + post-prune eval for RASP and Standard. Map threshold where both collapse.\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_postprune: 0.10\n      standard_30_postprune: 0.06\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.30\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n      both_below_threshold: true\n    result_rationale: \"30%已完成pruning（registry: prune_rasp_30 actual=28.7%, prune_standard_30 actual=28.5%）。Post-prune eval预期：两者均严重受损但RASP略好。30%接近D005中35% total collapse的阈值，EOS rate极低表明模型结构被严重破坏。RASP 10% > Standard 6%因为CKA-aware selection即使在极端稀疏度下仍能identify最核心的非冗余结构。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Sparsity Threshold Mapping\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, RASP Post-Prune, Standard Post-Prune, EOS Rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", \"29%\", \"27%\", \">90%\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"21%\", \"16%\", \"56-70%\"]\n          - [\"30%\", \"10%\", \"6%\", \"15-30%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: accuracy degradation curve across sparsity levels. Both methods approach zero around 30-35%. The gap widens then narrows as both collapse.\"\n    analysis: \"30%标定了'structural death zone'。两者均不可SFT恢复至实用水平（预期<35%），确认paper focus on 20-25%的合理性。提供sparsity-accuracy曲线的第三个数据点。\"\n\n  - name: \"Extended evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks to show generalization beyond GSM8K\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.52\n      rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n      rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n      standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.50\n      standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n      standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n      unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.63\n      unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n    result_rationale: \"OOD eval确认SFT recovery不是GSM8K memorization。RASP在所有benchmarks上marginal advantage（1-2pp）与GSM8K pattern一致。MMLU保留较多因为knowledge存储在unpruned layers。HumanEval和MATH-500降幅更大因为需要更多compositional reasoning chains（被pruning破坏）。Unpruned→Pruned的gap在MATH-500最大因为multi-step reasoning最依赖structural integrity。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-Benchmark Evaluation\"\n        columns: [Config, GSM8K, MATH-500, HumanEval, MMLU]\n        rows:\n          - [Unpruned, \"81.3%\", \"52%\", \"55%\", \"63%\"]\n          - [RASP_20 SFT, \"61.5%\", \"28%\", \"35%\", \"52%\"]\n          - [Standard_20 SFT, \"59.3%\", \"26%\", \"33%\", \"50%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: 4 benchmarks × 3 configs, showing proportional degradation pattern is consistent\"\n    analysis: \"OOD generalization确认recovery是genuine reasoning restoration而非pattern memorization。RASP advantage跨benchmark一致但不dramatic，支持'marginal SFT advantage'的honest framing。\"\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Gradient-free structured pruning (ICML 2025) at 20%. Full pipeline comparison.\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_20_postprune: 0.22\n      bonsai_20_sft_accuracy: 0.53\n      bonsai_20_grpo_collapse_step: 35\n      bonsai_20_grpo_peak_reward: 0.048\n    result_rationale: \"Bonsai uses activation-based structural importance (no gradients)，比magnitude-only好但比gradient-based差。Post-prune 22%介于random(15%)和Standard(27%)之间。SFT recovery 53%低于Standard因为activation-based scoring在reasoning model上不如gradient-based。GRPO collapse在step 35——比RASP(10)慢但比Standard(60)快，因为Bonsai的importance metric不像Standard那样隐式保留冗余路径。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: All Baselines Comparison\"\n        columns: [Method, Type, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, \"CKA-aware\", \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"step 10\"]\n          - [Standard, \"Importance\", \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"step 60\"]\n          - [GRASPrune, \"Gradient budget\", \"7%\", \"41%\", \"step 3\"]\n          - [Bonsai, \"Activation\", \"22%\", \"53%\", \"step 35\"]\n          - [Random, \"None\", \"15%\", \"42%\", \"step 8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: SFT recovery (x) vs GRPO collapse step (y) for all 5 methods. Shows inverse relationship for methods that remove more redundancy.\"\n    analysis: \"5-method comparison构建完整的方法landscape。关键洞见：collapse step与SFT accuracy不是简单正相关——RASP有最高SFT但最快collapse，验证Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff不是artifact of binary comparison。\"\n\n  - name: \"CKA reliability analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Split-half consistency and calibration size sensitivity for CKA scoring\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.94\n      split_half_p_value: 0.0001\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.91\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.96\n      cal_256_accuracy: 0.28\n      cal_512_accuracy: 0.31\n      cal_1024_accuracy: 0.31\n      optimal_cal_size: 512\n    result_rationale: \"CKA measures structural similarity which is a stable property of the network（不像gradient那样sample-dependent）。Split-half ρ=0.94表明CKA scoring高度reproducible。256→512有accuracy提升因为更好估计layer-wise statistics，但512→1024饱和因为CKA kernel已收敛。这证明RASP不需要大量calibration data，512 samples足够。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CKA Stability Analysis\"\n        columns: [Cal Size, Accuracy, Rank Corr vs 512]\n        rows:\n          - [256, \"28%\", 0.91]\n          - [512, \"31%\", 1.00]\n          - [1024, \"31%\", 0.96]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Left: split-half rank correlation histogram (bootstrapped). Right: accuracy vs calibration size curve showing saturation at 512.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA scoring is stable and efficient。reviewer concern about calibration sensitivity addressed: 512 samples sufficient, split-half ρ>0.9。\"\n\n  - name: \"α sensitivity ablation (post-SFT)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} with full SFT recovery. Paper's single free parameter.\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n      alpha_0.25_sft_accuracy: 0.58\n      alpha_0.5_sft_accuracy: 0.59\n      alpha_1.0_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n      alpha_2.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n      alpha_4.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n      optimal_alpha: 1.0\n      u_shape_confirmed: true\n      grpo_collapse_alpha_0: 55\n      grpo_collapse_alpha_1: 10\n      grpo_collapse_alpha_2: 7\n    result_rationale: \"α=0时S(h)=I(h)（Standard），α→∞时S(h)∝(1-F(h))^α（纯CKA，忽略importance）。已有post-prune data showing U-shape：α∈{0,0.25,0.5}≈22-27%，α≥1.0达31-36%。Post-SFT pattern：α=0等同Standard (59.3%)，α=1.0是RASP (61.5%)最优平衡，α=2.0略提升post-prune(36%)但SFT recovery与α=1相当（redundancy过度惩罚导致剪掉一些SFT需要的结构）。GRPO collapse速度：α越大→越多redundancy被移除→collapse越快。α=0(Standard)≈step55（接近v8的60），α=1(RASP)=step10（v9数据），α=2约step7。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: α Sensitivity (20% sparsity, N=1319)\"\n        columns: [α, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0, \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"step ~55\"]\n          - [0.25, \"23%\", \"58%\", \"step ~50\"]\n          - [0.5, \"22%\", \"59%\", \"step ~45\"]\n          - [1.0, \"31%\", \"61.5%\", \"step ~10\"]\n          - [2.0, \"36%\", \"62%\", \"step ~7\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-panel: (A) Post-prune accuracy vs α (U-shape). (B) Post-SFT accuracy vs α (monotonic increase from α=0.5). (C) GRPO collapse step vs α (monotonic decrease). Shows SFT and GRPO optimization directions are opposed.\"\n    analysis: \"α controls redundancy-importance tradeoff。Panel C是核心：α越大SFT越好但GRPO越不稳定——这就是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在连续parameter space中的表达。α是tuning knob，不是hyperparameter gamble。\"\n\n  - name: \"Inference speedup benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Wall-clock latency and throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms: 45\n      rasp_20_latency_ms: 37\n      standard_20_latency_ms: 37\n      speedup_ratio: 1.22\n      dense_throughput_tps: 85\n      rasp_20_throughput_tps: 104\n      standard_20_throughput_tps: 104\n      memory_reduction_pct: 19\n      batch_size: 1\n      seq_len: 512\n    result_rationale: \"20%结构化剪枝移除~19%参数（实际sparsity 19%，见registry）。结构化剪枝直接减少矩阵维度，无需专用sparse kernel。理论加速1/(1-0.19)=1.23×，实际~1.22×因为attention和layer norm不被pruned。RASP和Standard speedup相同因为它们移除相同数量的参数（只是选择不同structures）。Memory reduction与parameter reduction线性对应。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Inference Efficiency\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Params (B)\", \"Latency (ms)\", \"Throughput (tok/s)\", \"Memory (GB)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, \"7.62B\", 45, 85, 15.2]\n          - [RASP_20, \"6.17B\", 37, 104, 12.3]\n          - [Standard_20, \"6.17B\", 37, 104, 12.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing latency/throughput across configs. Both pruned methods identical, ~22% faster than dense.\"\n    analysis: \"Structured pruning delivers real wallclock speedup without custom kernels。Efficiency是pruning的practical motivation，但不是paper核心contribution——放在appendix或supplementary。\"\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured pruning baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20% for Self-Healing comparison calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_postprune: 0.55\n      unstructured_20_sft_accuracy: 0.72\n      unstructured_20_grpo_collapse_step: null\n      unstructured_20_grpo_reward_final: 0.35\n      unstructured_20_grpo_no_collapse: true\n      unstructured_vs_structured_gap: 25\n    result_rationale: \"Unstructured pruning at 20% damage远小于structured（保留所有neuron/head，仅零化individual weights）。Post-prune 55%（vs structured 27-29%）因为network topology完整。SFT recovery至72%因为functional capacity largely preserved。GRPO不collapse因为exploration paths完整——这正是structured pruning unique failure的对照。Self-Healing claims RLVR works at 25% unstructured → 我们的数据应与其一致：unstructured pruning不触发collapse。这calibrates paper的claim为'structured pruning specific'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured at 20%\"\n        columns: [Pruning Type, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Status]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Structured (RASP)\", \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"Collapse step 10\"]\n          - [\"Structured (Standard)\", \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"Collapse step 60\"]\n          - [\"Unstructured (Magnitude)\", \"55%\", \"72%\", \"No collapse\"]\n          - [\"Dense (Unpruned)\", \"81.3%\", \"81.3%\", \"No collapse\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Collapse dynamics plot: unstructured pruning curve overlaps with unpruned (both stable), while structured methods show distinct collapse patterns\"\n    analysis: \"Key differentiation vs Self-Healing: GRPO failure是structural pruning特有的。Unstructured pruning保留all pathway topology，RL exploration不受限。Paper claim narrowed to 'structured pruning causes GRPO collapse'——更精确，更defensible。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD eval contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Standard_20 SFT model (59.3% GSM8K) evaluated on MATH-500 and HumanEval\"\n    expected_results:\n      standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n      standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n      rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n      rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n      ratio_gsm8k_to_math500_standard: 2.28\n      memorization_ruled_out: true\n    result_rationale: \"Standard SFT 1%→59.3%(GSM8K)的jump在OOD benchmarks上应按比例衰减但不崩溃。MATH-500比GSM8K难~2×，所以59.3% GSM8K → ~26% MATH-500合理。如果是纯memorization则MATH-500应≈random(~5%)。26%远高于random，确认genuine reasoning recovery。RASP在OOD上保持2pp advantage与GSM8K pattern一致。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OOD Generalization Check\"\n        columns: [Config, GSM8K, MATH-500, HumanEval]\n        rows:\n          - [Standard_20 SFT, \"59.3%\", \"26%\", \"33%\"]\n          - [RASP_20 SFT, \"61.5%\", \"28%\", \"35%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bars showing consistent RASP advantage across benchmarks, ruling out GSM8K-specific overfitting\"\n    analysis: \"Contingency experiment结果positive：OOD performance confirms SFT recovery is genuine。Standard的1%→59.3%不是memorization artifact。Best tier下此experiment是supplementary evidence而非必需。\"\n\n  # Cross-model experiments (Qwen-Math-7B, part of scope expansion)\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse replication (20%)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_20\"\n    description: \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B pruned models to replicate collapse severity gradient on second model\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n      qwen_standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n      qwen_rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n      qwen_standard_20_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n      qwen_collapse_ratio: 5.6\n      qwen_rasp_grpo_peak_reward: 0.030\n      qwen_standard_grpo_peak_reward: 0.055\n      cross_model_pattern_replicated: true\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen-Math-7B SFT accuracy已知(RASP 72.5%, Standard 71%)。GRPO collapse应replicate severity gradient：RASP更快collapse因为CKA-aware selection移除了更多冗余路径。但Qwen-Math的baseline更强（math-specific pretraining），所以collapse略慢于DeepSeek-R1模型（step8 vs step10 for RASP）但比例关系保持。Collapse ratio 5.6×(45/8)与DeepSeek的6×(60/10)相当，验证跨模型一致性。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Model Collapse Comparison\"\n        columns: [Model, \"RASP Collapse\", \"Standard Collapse\", Ratio]\n        rows:\n          - [DeepSeek-R1-7B, \"step 10\", \"step 60\", \"6×\"]\n          - [Qwen-Math-7B, \"step 8\", \"step 45\", \"5.6×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side collapse dynamics (frac_zero_std) for both models, showing parallel patterns with similar ratios\"\n    analysis: \"跨模型复现是best tier的核心要求。Ratio在5-6×范围内一致证明Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff是general principle而非model-specific artifact。\"\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO collapse\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_25\"\n    description: \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B at 25% sparsity. Tests collapse acceleration on second model.\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n      qwen_standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n      qwen_rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step: 3\n      qwen_standard_25_grpo_collapse_step: 18\n      qwen_25_collapse_ratio: 6.0\n      sft_gap_qwen_25_pp: 1.0\n      cross_model_collapse_acceleration: true\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen-Math 25% SFT已知(RASP 64%, Standard 63%, gap仅1pp)。GRPO collapse进一步加速：RASP step3(vs 20%的step8)，Standard step18(vs 20%的step45)。Acceleration factor ~2.5×与DeepSeek pattern(step4 vs step10)一致。注意Qwen-Math上SFT gap不显著(1pp)但collapse gradient依然清晰——这强化了'RASP对GRPO有害'的claim不依赖于SFT优势的大小。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Qwen-Math Sparsity × Method × Recovery\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, Method, SFT, GRPO Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", RASP, \"72.5%\", \"step 8\"]\n          - [\"20%\", Standard, \"71%\", \"step 45\"]\n          - [\"25%\", RASP, \"64%\", \"step 3\"]\n          - [\"25%\", Standard, \"63%\", \"step 18\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 grid of collapse curves: rows=sparsity(20/25), cols=model(DeepSeek/Qwen). All four panels show same RASP<Standard pattern.\"\n    analysis: \"四个condition(2 models × 2 sparsities)全部replicate collapse severity gradient。这是paper最强的generalization evidence。即使SFT gap在Qwen上不显著，GRPO collapse diagnostic依然robust——strengthens Claim 2 (collapse as diagnostic tool)。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2171,"cache_read_input_tokens":31708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2171},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab5731f7-b47d-4dab-9a71-8ef9ffe1cf05","uuid":"de14e79c-1cb8-4b63-87b4-22079664cc07"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":238277,"duration_api_ms":240166,"num_turns":2,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: \"25%稀疏度放大SFT gap至显著水平，GRPO collapse在两个模型上均加速，三条claim完整成立。RASP既是SFT最优方法又是RLVR collapse诊断工具，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff跨模型跨稀疏度一致。投EMNLP Main无需降档。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K eval baseline + pruned models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"N=1319 full eval for unpruned baseline, RASP_20 post-prune, Standard_20 post-prune\"\n    expected_results:\n      unpruned_baseline_accuracy: 0.8127\n      rasp_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.29\n      standard_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.27\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 2.0\n      n_total: 1319\n    result_rationale: \"已有N=100数据确认RASP 31% vs Standard 27%。N=1319仅收窄CI（±2.4pp），点估计不变。Post-prune gap ~2pp不显著，因为pruning damage尚未通过SFT recovery放大差异。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Post-Prune Accuracy (20% structured, N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Model, Accuracy, 95% CI]\n        rows:\n          - [Unpruned, \"81.27%\", \"±2.1pp\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"29.0%\", \"±2.4pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"±2.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing massive accuracy drop from pruning (81→29/27%) with overlapping CIs between RASP and Standard\"\n    analysis: \"Post-prune差异不显著证实pruning damage本身不区分方法，真正差异在recovery阶段才显现。\"\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K eval all recovered models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"N=1319 eval for RASP_20 SFT, Standard_20 SFT, RASP_20 GRPO, Standard_20 GRPO, unpruned GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n      standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n      rasp_20_grpo_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n      standard_20_grpo_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n      unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n      sft_gap_rasp_vs_standard_pp: 2.2\n      grpo_delta_rasp_pp: -0.84\n      grpo_delta_standard_pp: -0.38\n      grpo_delta_unpruned_pp: 0.0\n    result_rationale: \"已有完整数据。GRPO对所有模型accuracy无正增益（unpruned完全相同1072/1319），pruned模型略降。paper Table 1核心数据已齐全。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Recovery Accuracy (GSM8K, N=1319, greedy)\"\n        columns: [Config, SFT, GRPO, \"Δ(GRPO-SFT)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Unpruned, \"81.27%\", \"81.27%\", \"+0.00pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"59.29%\", \"58.91%\", \"-0.38pp\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"61.49%\", \"60.65%\", \"-0.84pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for 3 configs, showing GRPO never improves accuracy\"\n    analysis: \"GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling是universal的；pruning-specific failure是training collapse而非accuracy degradation。\"\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune baseline 20% full pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO. ACL 2026 SOTA external baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      postprune_accuracy: 0.07\n      postprune_eos_rate: 0.02\n      post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n      post_sft_stderr: 0.027\n      post_sft_n1319_accuracy: 0.40\n      grpo_collapse_step: 3\n      grpo_peak_reward: 0.012\n      grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n    result_rationale: \"GRASP post-prune仅7%（已验证），SFT恢复至41%（已验证，p=0.001 vs Standard 64%）。GRASP激进剪枝破坏更多结构冗余，GRPO应在≤5步collapse——比RASP更快。GRASP removes high-gradient structures regardless of functional redundancy，resulting in maximal RLVR instability。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse Step]\n        rows:\n          - [GRASPrune, \"7%\", \"41%\", \"~3\"]\n          - [RASP, \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"~10\"]\n          - [Standard, \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"~60\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Collapse dynamics 4-line plot: GRASPrune(step3) < RASP(step10) < Standard(step60) < Unpruned(never). 严重度梯度完整。\"\n    analysis: \"GRASPrune的gradient-based选择策略去除了最多functional redundancy，验证了collapse速度∝redundancy removal程度。四点梯度使诊断工具framing更convincing。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune evaluation with 5 seeds for robust variance estimation\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.295\n      rasp_20_std: 0.012\n      standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.270\n      standard_20_std: 0.015\n      rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.03\n      seeds: [42, 123, 456, 789, 1024]\n      n_per_seed: 1319\n    result_rationale: \"Post-prune eval是deterministic（greedy decoding），seed影响仅来自calibration data sampling。RASP的CKA scoring对calibration data更稳定（因为CKA captures structural而非instance-level信号），故std略低。5-seed下2.5pp gap可达p<0.05。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Accuracy\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Mean±Std\", \"95% CI\", Seeds]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, \"29.5±1.2%\", \"[27.1, 31.9]\", 5]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0±1.5%\", \"[24.0, 30.0]\", 5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot with 5 seeds per method, showing RASP略高且方差更小\"\n    analysis: \"Post-prune gap达到marginal significance (p=0.03)，但核心论点不依赖此——真正差异在recovery和collapse dynamics。Multi-seed确认pruning本身reproducible。\"\n\n  - name: \"Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Ablation pruning at 20%: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random. Isolate CKA contribution\"\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_postprune: 0.25\n      gradient_only_postprune: 0.28\n      random_postprune: 0.15\n      magnitude_sft_recovery: 0.56\n      gradient_sft_recovery: 0.58\n      random_sft_recovery: 0.42\n      magnitude_grpo_collapse_step: 40\n      gradient_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n      random_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n    result_rationale: \"Magnitude-only保留大权重但忽略功能冗余，post-prune与Standard(importance-based)接近。Gradient-only与GRASPrune逻辑相似但无budget约束，略好于magnitude。Random是lower bound。CKA的贡献在于：RASP(31%)>gradient(28%)>magnitude(25%)>random(15%)。GRPO collapse速度中，random最快（随机破坏冗余路径），magnitude/gradient因保留high-importance units而较慢，但仍比Standard快（Standard的importance metric隐式保留了部分冗余）。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Scoring Ablation Results\"\n        columns: [Scoring, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP (I×(1-F)^α), \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"step ~10\"]\n          - [Standard (importance), \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"step ~60\"]\n          - [Gradient-only, \"28%\", \"58%\", \"step ~45\"]\n          - [Magnitude-only, \"25%\", \"56%\", \"step ~40\"]\n          - [Random, \"15%\", \"42%\", \"step ~8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: post-prune accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all methods, showing RASP is Pareto-dominated point — high SFT but fast collapse\"\n    analysis: \"CKA贡献体现在SFT recovery（+5pp over magnitude），但对GRPO有害（collapse比magnitude/gradient快4-6×）。验证redundancy removal与collapse速度的因果关系。\"\n\n  - name: \"Per-structure CKA-recoverability correlation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"Per-head F(h) correlated with activation change post-recovery. Mixed-effects regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      fh_recovery_correlation_sft: -0.42\n      fh_recovery_correlation_sft_p: 0.001\n      fh_collapse_speed_correlation: 0.55\n      fh_collapse_speed_p: 0.0003\n      mixed_effects_r2: 0.38\n      layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n      controlling_for_weight_norm: true\n      controlling_for_gradient_importance: true\n      n_structures: 784\n    result_rationale: \"F(h)（CKA功能冗余度）高的结构在SFT后activation变化小（r=-0.42）——因为它们的功能已由其他结构承接，不需要恢复。但高F(h)结构的移除与GRPO collapse速度正相关（r=0.55）——因为它们提供的backup paths是RL exploration的安全网。Mixed-effects R²=0.38说明F(h)解释了显著但非全部方差（其他因素如layer position也重要）。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CKA-Recoverability Regression\"\n        columns: [Predictor, β, SE, p-value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\", -0.42, 0.08, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"Weight norm\", 0.12, 0.05, 0.02]\n          - [\"Gradient importance\", 0.08, 0.06, 0.18]\n          - [\"Layer (random)\", \"σ²=0.15\", \"-\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter with regression line: F(h) vs activation change magnitude (left panel, SFT context), F(h) vs time-to-collapse contribution (right panel, GRPO context)\"\n    analysis: \"机制验证：高冗余结构SFT可安全移除（功能可redistribution），但GRPO需要它们作为exploration buffer。这是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的结构层面证据。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT-only recovery comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Same pruned models, SFT only (no GRPO stage). Tests whether pruning strategy优劣在SFT-only pipeline中成立\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.6149\n      standard_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5929\n      gap_pp: 2.2\n      p_value: 0.25\n      rasp_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.57\n      standard_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5125\n      gap_25_pp: 5.75\n      p_25_value: 0.008\n    result_rationale: \"20%稀疏度下SFT gap仅2.2pp（已有数据，p=0.25不显著）。25%稀疏度放大效应：Standard在更高稀疏度下丢失更多关键结构，SFT难以完全恢复；RASP的CKA-aware选择在25%时保留了更关键的functional units，使recovery gap扩大至5.75pp（p=0.008）。这验证了'SFT下RASP优越性随稀疏度单调递增'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SFT-Only Recovery by Sparsity\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, RASP SFT, Standard SFT, Gap, p-value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", \"61.49%\", \"59.29%\", \"+2.2pp\", 0.25]\n          - [\"25%\", \"57.0%\", \"51.25%\", \"+5.75pp\", 0.008]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: accuracy vs sparsity for RASP and Standard, diverging as sparsity increases. Error bars show CI narrowing at N=1319.\"\n    analysis: \"SFT gap在25%处achieve significance。Claim 3直接支持：SFT-only pipeline下RASP显著优于Standard，但GRPO pipeline下RASP有害——pruning策略的最优性conditioned on recovery method。\"\n\n  - name: \"25% sparsity full pipeline (RASP + Standard)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25% structured pruning: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both methods. Core scope expansion.\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_postprune: 0.21\n      standard_25_postprune: 0.16\n      rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.57\n      standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n      sft_gap_pp: 5.75\n      sft_gap_p_value: 0.008\n      grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n      grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.025\n      grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.97\n      grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 20\n      grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.055\n      grpo_standard_25_step60_frac_zero_std: 0.85\n      collapse_ratio_standard_vs_rasp: 5.0\n    result_rationale: \"25%稀疏度下两个关键放大效应：(1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大至5.75pp，因为Standard在更高稀疏度下不得不移除更多functionally important structures（importance ranking的long tail quality下降），而RASP的CKA-aware selection依然能识别truly redundant structures。(2) GRPO collapse加速：RASP从step10→step4（冗余路径更少，RL exploration更快失去safety net），Standard从step60→step20（相同逻辑但程度较轻）。Collapse ratio从6x(20%)收缩至5x(25%)因为Standard也开始受损严重。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 25% Sparsity Pipeline Results\"\n        columns: [Method, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse, GRPO Δ vs SFT]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_25, \"21%\", \"57.0%\", \"step 4\", \"-1.5pp\"]\n          - [Standard_25, \"16%\", \"51.25%\", \"step 20\", \"-2.0pp\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Collapse Dynamics Comparison (20% vs 25%)\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Collapse@20%\", \"Collapse@25%\", Acceleration]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, \"step 10\", \"step 4\", \"2.5×\"]\n          - [Standard, \"step 60\", \"step 20\", \"3×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel: (Left) SFT accuracy vs sparsity showing divergence at 25%. (Right) frac_zero_std curves at 25% showing RASP collapse at step 4 vs Standard at step 20.\"\n    analysis: \"25%是paper的sweet spot：SFT gap达到显著，GRPO collapse更极端，所有效应放大。这使三条claim全部有strong statistical backing。\"\n\n  - name: \"30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30% prune + post-prune eval for RASP and Standard. Map threshold where both collapse.\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_postprune: 0.10\n      standard_30_postprune: 0.06\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.30\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n      both_below_threshold: true\n    result_rationale: \"30%已完成pruning（registry: prune_rasp_30 actual=28.7%, prune_standard_30 actual=28.5%）。Post-prune eval预期：两者均严重受损但RASP略好。30%接近D005中35% total collapse的阈值，EOS rate极低表明模型结构被严重破坏。RASP 10% > Standard 6%因为CKA-aware selection即使在极端稀疏度下仍能identify最核心的非冗余结构。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Sparsity Threshold Mapping\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, RASP Post-Prune, Standard Post-Prune, EOS Rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", \"29%\", \"27%\", \">90%\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"21%\", \"16%\", \"56-70%\"]\n          - [\"30%\", \"10%\", \"6%\", \"15-30%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: accuracy degradation curve across sparsity levels. Both methods approach zero around 30-35%. The gap widens then narrows as both collapse.\"\n    analysis: \"30%标定了'structural death zone'。两者均不可SFT恢复至实用水平（预期<35%），确认paper focus on 20-25%的合理性。提供sparsity-accuracy曲线的第三个数据点。\"\n\n  - name: \"Extended evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks to show generalization beyond GSM8K\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.52\n      rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n      rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n      standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.50\n      standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n      standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n      unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.63\n      unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n    result_rationale: \"OOD eval确认SFT recovery不是GSM8K memorization。RASP在所有benchmarks上marginal advantage（1-2pp）与GSM8K pattern一致。MMLU保留较多因为knowledge存储在unpruned layers。HumanEval和MATH-500降幅更大因为需要更多compositional reasoning chains（被pruning破坏）。Unpruned→Pruned的gap在MATH-500最大因为multi-step reasoning最依赖structural integrity。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-Benchmark Evaluation\"\n        columns: [Config, GSM8K, MATH-500, HumanEval, MMLU]\n        rows:\n          - [Unpruned, \"81.3%\", \"52%\", \"55%\", \"63%\"]\n          - [RASP_20 SFT, \"61.5%\", \"28%\", \"35%\", \"52%\"]\n          - [Standard_20 SFT, \"59.3%\", \"26%\", \"33%\", \"50%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: 4 benchmarks × 3 configs, showing proportional degradation pattern is consistent\"\n    analysis: \"OOD generalization确认recovery是genuine reasoning restoration而非pattern memorization。RASP advantage跨benchmark一致但不dramatic，支持'marginal SFT advantage'的honest framing。\"\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Gradient-free structured pruning (ICML 2025) at 20%. Full pipeline comparison.\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_20_postprune: 0.22\n      bonsai_20_sft_accuracy: 0.53\n      bonsai_20_grpo_collapse_step: 35\n      bonsai_20_grpo_peak_reward: 0.048\n    result_rationale: \"Bonsai uses activation-based structural importance (no gradients)，比magnitude-only好但比gradient-based差。Post-prune 22%介于random(15%)和Standard(27%)之间。SFT recovery 53%低于Standard因为activation-based scoring在reasoning model上不如gradient-based。GRPO collapse在step 35——比RASP(10)慢但比Standard(60)快，因为Bonsai的importance metric不像Standard那样隐式保留冗余路径。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: All Baselines Comparison\"\n        columns: [Method, Type, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, \"CKA-aware\", \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"step 10\"]\n          - [Standard, \"Importance\", \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"step 60\"]\n          - [GRASPrune, \"Gradient budget\", \"7%\", \"41%\", \"step 3\"]\n          - [Bonsai, \"Activation\", \"22%\", \"53%\", \"step 35\"]\n          - [Random, \"None\", \"15%\", \"42%\", \"step 8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: SFT recovery (x) vs GRPO collapse step (y) for all 5 methods. Shows inverse relationship for methods that remove more redundancy.\"\n    analysis: \"5-method comparison构建完整的方法landscape。关键洞见：collapse step与SFT accuracy不是简单正相关——RASP有最高SFT但最快collapse，验证Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff不是artifact of binary comparison。\"\n\n  - name: \"CKA reliability analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Split-half consistency and calibration size sensitivity for CKA scoring\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.94\n      split_half_p_value: 0.0001\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.91\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.96\n      cal_256_accuracy: 0.28\n      cal_512_accuracy: 0.31\n      cal_1024_accuracy: 0.31\n      optimal_cal_size: 512\n    result_rationale: \"CKA measures structural similarity which is a stable property of the network（不像gradient那样sample-dependent）。Split-half ρ=0.94表明CKA scoring高度reproducible。256→512有accuracy提升因为更好估计layer-wise statistics，但512→1024饱和因为CKA kernel已收敛。这证明RASP不需要大量calibration data，512 samples足够。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CKA Stability Analysis\"\n        columns: [Cal Size, Accuracy, Rank Corr vs 512]\n        rows:\n          - [256, \"28%\", 0.91]\n          - [512, \"31%\", 1.00]\n          - [1024, \"31%\", 0.96]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Left: split-half rank correlation histogram (bootstrapped). Right: accuracy vs calibration size curve showing saturation at 512.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA scoring is stable and efficient。reviewer concern about calibration sensitivity addressed: 512 samples sufficient, split-half ρ>0.9。\"\n\n  - name: \"α sensitivity ablation (post-SFT)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} with full SFT recovery. Paper's single free parameter.\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n      alpha_0.25_sft_accuracy: 0.58\n      alpha_0.5_sft_accuracy: 0.59\n      alpha_1.0_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n      alpha_2.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n      alpha_4.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n      optimal_alpha: 1.0\n      u_shape_confirmed: true\n      grpo_collapse_alpha_0: 55\n      grpo_collapse_alpha_1: 10\n      grpo_collapse_alpha_2: 7\n    result_rationale: \"α=0时S(h)=I(h)（Standard），α→∞时S(h)∝(1-F(h))^α（纯CKA，忽略importance）。已有post-prune data showing U-shape：α∈{0,0.25,0.5}≈22-27%，α≥1.0达31-36%。Post-SFT pattern：α=0等同Standard (59.3%)，α=1.0是RASP (61.5%)最优平衡，α=2.0略提升post-prune(36%)但SFT recovery与α=1相当（redundancy过度惩罚导致剪掉一些SFT需要的结构）。GRPO collapse速度：α越大→越多redundancy被移除→collapse越快。α=0(Standard)≈step55（接近v8的60），α=1(RASP)=step10（v9数据），α=2约step7。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: α Sensitivity (20% sparsity, N=1319)\"\n        columns: [α, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0, \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"step ~55\"]\n          - [0.25, \"23%\", \"58%\", \"step ~50\"]\n          - [0.5, \"22%\", \"59%\", \"step ~45\"]\n          - [1.0, \"31%\", \"61.5%\", \"step ~10\"]\n          - [2.0, \"36%\", \"62%\", \"step ~7\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-panel: (A) Post-prune accuracy vs α (U-shape). (B) Post-SFT accuracy vs α (monotonic increase from α=0.5). (C) GRPO collapse step vs α (monotonic decrease). Shows SFT and GRPO optimization directions are opposed.\"\n    analysis: \"α controls redundancy-importance tradeoff。Panel C是核心：α越大SFT越好但GRPO越不稳定——这就是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在连续parameter space中的表达。α是tuning knob，不是hyperparameter gamble。\"\n\n  - name: \"Inference speedup benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Wall-clock latency and throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms: 45\n      rasp_20_latency_ms: 37\n      standard_20_latency_ms: 37\n      speedup_ratio: 1.22\n      dense_throughput_tps: 85\n      rasp_20_throughput_tps: 104\n      standard_20_throughput_tps: 104\n      memory_reduction_pct: 19\n      batch_size: 1\n      seq_len: 512\n    result_rationale: \"20%结构化剪枝移除~19%参数（实际sparsity 19%，见registry）。结构化剪枝直接减少矩阵维度，无需专用sparse kernel。理论加速1/(1-0.19)=1.23×，实际~1.22×因为attention和layer norm不被pruned。RASP和Standard speedup相同因为它们移除相同数量的参数（只是选择不同structures）。Memory reduction与parameter reduction线性对应。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Inference Efficiency\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Params (B)\", \"Latency (ms)\", \"Throughput (tok/s)\", \"Memory (GB)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, \"7.62B\", 45, 85, 15.2]\n          - [RASP_20, \"6.17B\", 37, 104, 12.3]\n          - [Standard_20, \"6.17B\", 37, 104, 12.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing latency/throughput across configs. Both pruned methods identical, ~22% faster than dense.\"\n    analysis: \"Structured pruning delivers real wallclock speedup without custom kernels。Efficiency是pruning的practical motivation，但不是paper核心contribution——放在appendix或supplementary。\"\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured pruning baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20% for Self-Healing comparison calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_postprune: 0.55\n      unstructured_20_sft_accuracy: 0.72\n      unstructured_20_grpo_collapse_step: null\n      unstructured_20_grpo_reward_final: 0.35\n      unstructured_20_grpo_no_collapse: true\n      unstructured_vs_structured_gap: 25\n    result_rationale: \"Unstructured pruning at 20% damage远小于structured（保留所有neuron/head，仅零化individual weights）。Post-prune 55%（vs structured 27-29%）因为network topology完整。SFT recovery至72%因为functional capacity largely preserved。GRPO不collapse因为exploration paths完整——这正是structured pruning unique failure的对照。Self-Healing claims RLVR works at 25% unstructured → 我们的数据应与其一致：unstructured pruning不触发collapse。这calibrates paper的claim为'structured pruning specific'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured at 20%\"\n        columns: [Pruning Type, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, GRPO Status]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Structured (RASP)\", \"29%\", \"61.5%\", \"Collapse step 10\"]\n          - [\"Structured (Standard)\", \"27%\", \"59.3%\", \"Collapse step 60\"]\n          - [\"Unstructured (Magnitude)\", \"55%\", \"72%\", \"No collapse\"]\n          - [\"Dense (Unpruned)\", \"81.3%\", \"81.3%\", \"No collapse\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Collapse dynamics plot: unstructured pruning curve overlaps with unpruned (both stable), while structured methods show distinct collapse patterns\"\n    analysis: \"Key differentiation vs Self-Healing: GRPO failure是structural pruning特有的。Unstructured pruning保留all pathway topology，RL exploration不受限。Paper claim narrowed to 'structured pruning causes GRPO collapse'——更精确，更defensible。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD eval contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Standard_20 SFT model (59.3% GSM8K) evaluated on MATH-500 and HumanEval\"\n    expected_results:\n      standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n      standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n      rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n      rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n      ratio_gsm8k_to_math500_standard: 2.28\n      memorization_ruled_out: true\n    result_rationale: \"Standard SFT 1%→59.3%(GSM8K)的jump在OOD benchmarks上应按比例衰减但不崩溃。MATH-500比GSM8K难~2×，所以59.3% GSM8K → ~26% MATH-500合理。如果是纯memorization则MATH-500应≈random(~5%)。26%远高于random，确认genuine reasoning recovery。RASP在OOD上保持2pp advantage与GSM8K pattern一致。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OOD Generalization Check\"\n        columns: [Config, GSM8K, MATH-500, HumanEval]\n        rows:\n          - [Standard_20 SFT, \"59.3%\", \"26%\", \"33%\"]\n          - [RASP_20 SFT, \"61.5%\", \"28%\", \"35%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bars showing consistent RASP advantage across benchmarks, ruling out GSM8K-specific overfitting\"\n    analysis: \"Contingency experiment结果positive：OOD performance confirms SFT recovery is genuine。Standard的1%→59.3%不是memorization artifact。Best tier下此experiment是supplementary evidence而非必需。\"\n\n  # Cross-model experiments (Qwen-Math-7B, part of scope expansion)\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse replication (20%)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_20\"\n    description: \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B pruned models to replicate collapse severity gradient on second model\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n      qwen_standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n      qwen_rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n      qwen_standard_20_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n      qwen_collapse_ratio: 5.6\n      qwen_rasp_grpo_peak_reward: 0.030\n      qwen_standard_grpo_peak_reward: 0.055\n      cross_model_pattern_replicated: true\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen-Math-7B SFT accuracy已知(RASP 72.5%, Standard 71%)。GRPO collapse应replicate severity gradient：RASP更快collapse因为CKA-aware selection移除了更多冗余路径。但Qwen-Math的baseline更强（math-specific pretraining），所以collapse略慢于DeepSeek-R1模型（step8 vs step10 for RASP）但比例关系保持。Collapse ratio 5.6×(45/8)与DeepSeek的6×(60/10)相当，验证跨模型一致性。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Model Collapse Comparison\"\n        columns: [Model, \"RASP Collapse\", \"Standard Collapse\", Ratio]\n        rows:\n          - [DeepSeek-R1-7B, \"step 10\", \"step 60\", \"6×\"]\n          - [Qwen-Math-7B, \"step 8\", \"step 45\", \"5.6×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side collapse dynamics (frac_zero_std) for both models, showing parallel patterns with similar ratios\"\n    analysis: \"跨模型复现是best tier的核心要求。Ratio在5-6×范围内一致证明Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff是general principle而非model-specific artifact。\"\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO collapse\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_25\"\n    description: \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B at 25% sparsity. Tests collapse acceleration on second model.\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n      qwen_standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n      qwen_rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step: 3\n      qwen_standard_25_grpo_collapse_step: 18\n      qwen_25_collapse_ratio: 6.0\n      sft_gap_qwen_25_pp: 1.0\n      cross_model_collapse_acceleration: true\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen-Math 25% SFT已知(RASP 64%, Standard 63%, gap仅1pp)。GRPO collapse进一步加速：RASP step3(vs 20%的step8)，Standard step18(vs 20%的step45)。Acceleration factor ~2.5×与DeepSeek pattern(step4 vs step10)一致。注意Qwen-Math上SFT gap不显著(1pp)但collapse gradient依然清晰——这强化了'RASP对GRPO有害'的claim不依赖于SFT优势的大小。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Qwen-Math Sparsity × Method × Recovery\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, Method, SFT, GRPO Collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", RASP, \"72.5%\", \"step 8\"]\n          - [\"20%\", Standard, \"71%\", \"step 45\"]\n          - [\"25%\", RASP, \"64%\", \"step 3\"]\n          - [\"25%\", Standard, \"63%\", \"step 18\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 grid of collapse curves: rows=sparsity(20/25), cols=model(DeepSeek/Qwen). All four panels show same RASP<Standard pattern.\"\n    analysis: \"四个condition(2 models × 2 sparsities)全部replicate collapse severity gradient。这是paper最强的generalization evidence。即使SFT gap在Qwen上不显著，GRPO collapse diagnostic依然robust——strengthens Claim 2 (collapse as diagnostic tool)。\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ab5731f7-b47d-4dab-9a71-8ef9ffe1cf05","total_cost_usd":0.487618,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22038,"cache_read_input_tokens":43549,"output_tokens":12525,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22038,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":10461,"cache_read_input_tokens":31708,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2171},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":14821,"outputTokens":29,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.014966,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":12525,"cacheReadInputTokens":43549,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22038,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.47265199999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"aa0da213-fdcb-4a48-b860-4e3162fe3f19"}
